    "updated_at": "2026-11-15T23:41:15Z",
    "body": "fix on mkinney:issue/1468-chuck-options · PR #2083 · pinned by sim `lathe_chuck_jaws` (`outside_stepped_jaw_envelope_is_pinned`, `inside_grip_envelope_is_pinned`, `inside_stepped_jaw_envelope_is_pinned`, `step_nonsense_is_refused_by_name`, `inside_grip_nonsense_is_refused_by_name`, `a_file_from_before_reads_as_plain_outside_jaws`), app `lathe_chuck` (`inside_grip_jaws_are_steel_that_blocks_the_post`, `stepped_jaws_are_steel_where_they_stand_under_the_work`, `a_fit_seats_the_stock_on_the_step_and_refuses_an_inside_grip`), app `mcp_accessory`, ui `chuck_dialog_offers_fit_to_the_stock` and `chuck_fit_is_off_by_pose_for_an_inside_grip_and_square_stock` · merges at the next cut\n\nThe PR is a first slice (`Refs`, so merging it does not close this issue). It covers the \"Done means\" line: the dialog's \"Fit to the stock\", inside grip and stepped jaws with refusals by name and envelope tests, and the camcraft-mcp skill row.\n\nStill open here after it merges:\n\n- Independent 4-jaw offsets (each jaw's own radial position, off-centre work).\n- Chuck rpm limit feeding the workholding spindle-speed checks.\n- Chuck on a rotary axis of a milling setup (frame along the rotary axis).\n- Viewport look in the running app, with screenshots (the app was not launched for this PR).\n- A stock fit for an inside grip: it is refused by name today, because the stock (a box or a solid cylinder) does not state a bore.\n\nDecisions are in `docs/decisions/1468-chuck-options.md` on the branch.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
